{
  "_doc": "The technology tree. Each node: `industry` (a building type, or \"global\") picks its tab; `requires` lists nodes that must be finished first; `unlock` adds conditions. Step 70: an ordinary node opens at a player `level` (and after its `requires`); a Momo's letter proposing a node brings it early, as a discovery, never as a gate. A few nodes are `special` (the field says why): they keep a building `mastery` {type: level} or `proposal`: true (the letter itself opens it) -- leaves of the tree, so nothing ordinary waits on them. A node whose gate was once met stays discovered for good (across Prestige). Step 71: `industry` is the node's tab -- a discipline (farm, lumberyard, mine, research = the lab, power, global); smelting and car topics are modules of Mine, the studio of the Lab. Every tab holds a chain of at least eight tiers (a tier is 1 + the longest chain of prerequisites in the same tab), its gates rising along the chain; the screen shows what is open and what opens at the next level, not the whole tree (ResearchSystem.is_shown). {kind: power_output, multiply >= 1, type?} raises what generators of that type (or all) give. `cost` is paid when research starts (money, and items -- research notes come from the lab); `seconds` is how long it then takes, at a finished lab. `effects` are what it changes, as data the simulation applies and the UI describes: {kind: work|cooldown, type, action, multiply} scales a stage's active work or the wait after it (floors in the stage data still hold -- research never removes a required stage); {kind: yield, type, stage, item, add} adds to what a stage yields (fractions are rates, carried over exactly); {kind: research_time, multiply} scales how long research takes; {kind: auto, type, action} makes stages with that action run by themselves (a drip line waters; the waits stay); {kind: variety, type, variety} opens a crop variety for that building type; {kind: recipe, type, recipe} opens a recipe; {kind: batch, type, add} lets one charge hold more batches. `name`/`desc` are translation keys; desc explains the real technique. {kind: power_use, type, draw, multiply, required} makes that building draw `draw` kW while it works and, fully powered, work `multiply` times as long (a partly powered one in between); with `required` it cannot start without power. `branches` are research tabs that are not a building type. {kind: momo_work, multiply, type?} scales Momo work time (all types, or one). {kind: sale_price, multiply >= 1} raises what the daily sale pays (better market access); {kind: walk_speed, multiply >= 1} makes Momo walk faster. {kind: watch_tiles, add} lets every Momo watch `add` more tiles (4 -> 9 -> 16). An effect may list `per_level`: its multiply (or add) at levels 1, 2, ... exactly, instead of the balance.research.level_strength rule -- the numbers the points screen shows. {kind: route, strategy} opens a Momo routing strategy (auto: plan around waits).",
